menu "SdFat (vendored)"

config SDFAT_SCRATCH_IN_PSRAM
    bool "Allocate SdFat scratch buffers in PSRAM"
    default n
    help
        Moves the exFAT dual-FAT reseed chunk (16 KB) and the tail-cluster ring (~1 KB)
        out of internal .bss into a one-time heap allocation, PSRAM first (internal RAM if
        there is no PSRAM). Off = static arrays, identical to the vendored behaviour.
        Safe for the sdspi path: SdFat never hands these buffers to DMA; sdmmc copies
        through its own temporary DMA buffer. See port/sdfat_scratch.h.

endmenu
